id: SEC-026
title: Use-after-free / double-free patterns (Chrome V8 CVEs)
category: security
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .c .cpp .cc .h .hpp
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ .git/ build/
patterns:
  - regex: free\(\s*\w+\s*\)
    message: "free() without nulling pointer — use-after-free risk. Set pointer to NULL after free."
  - regex: delete\s+\w+;
    message: "delete without nulling pointer — use-after-free risk. Set to nullptr after delete."
fix: Set pointer to NULL/nullptr after free/delete. Better: use smart pointers (unique_ptr, shared_ptr) or RAII.